  "slug": "contract-terms-01-contrast",
  "title": "Clause from an auxiliary document, without a rule — clause linked and external text, side by side",
  "titleEs": "Cláusula incorporada — Comparación de dos supuestos",
  "category": "contract-terms",
  "categoryName": "Contenido y cláusulas",
  "motif": "Cláusula incorporada",
  "treatment": "contrast",
  "family": "paired-comparison",
  "description": "Two identical stages (two parties and their pigeonhole racks): in both, Party A's auxiliary document (●), a placeholder clause slip in its dock, travels to Party B, the clause station is reached and Party B's contract set (◆, at equal weight) then travels to Party A — at the same moments in both. The one changed fact is the supplied configuration: in A (clause linked, as supplied) Party B's hand moves the slip into the contract set's dock; in B (external text, as supplied) it stays in the auxiliary document's dock. The destination dock takes the same solid outline in each scene. A guide outlines the differing row of the comparison table; the key reads \"As supplied · no conclusion drawn\". No winner, no incorporation rule and no conclusion on whether the clause is part of anything.",
